## Context

Ticket 0552 (reading-1 item 14 follow-up) split into two aspects.
Aspect 1 — encoding — is DECIDED by the author (2026-06-12): the
canonical encoding is the literal Unicode em dash (—, U+2014), not the
LaTeX `---` ligature. Grounds: house style already mandates literal
Unicode glyphs in prose (.claude/rules/writing.md); guards and audits
become a plain grep (the 0543 waiver gap happened because the two
encodings diverge); the glyph is immune to fontspec/ligature-mapping
regressions.

Aspect 2 — whether to *restyle* (reduce the ~187 em dashes to commas,
colons, parentheses) — remains open in 0552 and is NOT this ticket.
This ticket is mechanical encoding conversion only: after it lands,
the em-dash count is unchanged but visible to a one-line grep.

## Relevant files

- `slides/manuscript/main.tex` — ~187 `---` occurrences in body prose
- `tests/test_manuscript_cohort_and_caveats.py` — existing abstract
  em-dash guard (knows about both encodings today)
- `.claude/rules/writing.md` — glyph convention (\newunicodechar
  preamble mappings for glyphs absent from the text font)

## Actions

1. Red test first (see Test below).
2. Sweep `main.tex`: replace prose `---` with the literal — glyph.
   Exclusions: verbatim/quote environments (the as-sent Doc-07 prompt
   block in Annex B is frozen quoted material — do NOT touch it; there
   is a drift guard on its text), LaTeX comments, any table or TikZ
   syntax where `-` runs are syntactic. Inspect each non-prose hit
   rather than blanket-sed.
3. Verify the rendering path: confirm the text font carries U+2014
   under tectonic; add a `\newunicodechar{—}{...}` preamble mapping
   ONLY if the build drops the glyph (follow the existing γ/ρ/τ
   pattern). The build must produce an identical-looking PDF.
4. Adherence guard: extend/add a test asserting `main.tex` contains no
   `---` outside the excluded environments, so the ligature encoding
   cannot creep back. Keep the existing abstract guard semantics.
5. Log the aspect-1 resolution in ticket 0552 (note, not close — its
   aspect 2 / restyle decision stays open, needs-human).

## Test

- Red step: a pytest (adherence-marked) that parses
  `slides/manuscript/main.tex`, strips verbatim/quote environments and
  comments, and asserts no `---` remains in prose. It must FAIL before
  the sweep (~187 hits) and PASS after.

## Verification

- [ ] `make -C slides manuscript` builds; em dashes render identically
      (spot-check a page in the PDF)
- [ ] Doc-07 prompt block byte-identical (its drift guard stays green)
- [ ] grep -c '—' main.tex ≈ prior `---` prose count (encoding moved,
      count unchanged)

## Invariants

- No prose rewording — this is encoding-only; aspect 2 (restyle) is
  0552's open decision
- `make check` green; existing adherence suite untouched semantics

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Prose `---` swept to — in main.tex, exclusions respected
- [ ] Adherence guard prevents `---` reintroduction in prose
- [ ] 0552 log notes aspect-1 resolution
- [ ] `make check` green
